  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A Zener diode of breakdown voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is used as a voltage regulator as shown in the figure. The current through the Zener diode is</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0035_e53767c54461.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 185px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0035_b0c84d26bda6.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 154px;\"/></p><p>As Zener is in breakdown region, therefore potential drop across it would be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. Now, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>200</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Also, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p>"
  }
}